# The one version of each toolchain, for the Mac, the Docker images and CI
# alike (the owner, 2026-11-09: "make it all consistent"). asdf's format,
# because CI's setup-python, setup-java and setup-node read it as their
# *-version-file, and mise or asdf on a Mac read it as it is. The rest
# reads it through scripts/build/toolchain.sh (`get <name>`), and what
# cannot read a file at all (a Dockerfile's FROM, the pom, the Gradle
# files, rust-toolchain.toml, .nvmrc) is written from it by
# `scripts/build/toolchain.sh`; `--check`, in CI's architecture job, fails
# on any place that differs. Bump a version here, run the script, commit
# what it changed.
java temurin-25
python 3.15.2
rust 1.99.1
nodejs 26
gradle 9.9.1
maven 3.10.0
# The .NET SDK of tools/msfs-agent (the MSFS replay agent): its global.json.
dotnet 11.0.100
# Below, tools mise and asdf do not install: read by this repo's scripts only.
xcode 27.2
# The Android NDK: the app's ndkVersion and engine/bindings/ffi/build-android.sh.
# One GitHub's ubuntu-26.04 runner image has installed, so CI downloads none.
android-ndk 30.0.16248370
# The Debian release every Debian-based image is built on (a -slim tag
# without one is the current release, trixie, by the same digest).
debian trixie
rust-edition 2024
